# Copilot for Devs

> A practical guide to using GitHub Copilot with structured interaction modes.

This repository contains practical prompts to use GitHub Copilot as a real development assistant, not just autocomplete.

## 🧠 Copilot Modes Covered

- **Agent** → autonomous code execution and implementation  
- **Ask** → explanations and diagnostics (read-only)  
- **Plan** → structured planning before coding  
- **Study** → guided learning and concept understanding  

## 📂 Structure

## 📂 Structure
prompts/
├── prompt-agent.md
├── prompt-ask.md
├── prompt-plan.md
└── prompt-study.md

## 🎯 Purpose

To explore how different AI interaction modes can improve:

- code quality  
- development speed  
- understanding of concepts  
- decision-making before implementation  

## 🚀 What I learned

- How to structure prompts professionally  
- Differences between AI modes (execution vs guidance)  
- Using AI as a developer assistant, not just a tool  
